{{Stealnotes
| name = Decoy
| desc = Requires acquiring {{A|Hoodwink|Sharpshooter}} in order for the {{M|illusion|text=Decoy illusion}} to channel Sharpshooter, else the illusion runs toward the nearest enemy unit.
}}
{{Draftnotes
| name = Decoy
| desc = Requires drafting {{Symbol|bonus agh}} {{A|Hoodwink|Sharpshooter}} to unlock this ability.<br><br>Does not require drafting {{A|Hoodwink|Bushwhack}} for its corresponding component to work.
}}

 {{Gamedesc
| image = {{#var:Decoy icon0}}
| desc = Hoodwink turns invisible, increasing her movement speed, and creates a decoy illusion that starts aiming a decreased damage Sharpshooter at the nearest enemy hero. If the illusion is attacked or hit by a targeted ability, it is destroyed and it throws a lesser bushwhack towards the enemy.
}}
* For ability component [[File:Dota2 Condition-3.png|3|21px]]:
** Neither offensive attacks nor offensive {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} unit-targeted abilities beyond the max distance procs {{A|Hoodwink|Bushwhack|text=Lesser Bushwhack}}.
** However, the {{Symbol|Target|Unit}} unit-targeted ability cast procs the {{M|Spell Block}} component.
** Offensive attacks still damage the Decoy-based [[illusion]] normally.

* Directly uses {{A|Hoodwink|Sharpshooter}}'s ability values, the Decoy-based [[illusion]] has the following additional properties:
** Neither requires {{A|Hoodwink|Bushwhack}} nor {{A|Hoodwink|Scurry}} to be learned.
** {{Symbol|Decoy}} {{Symbol|Illusions}} {{to}} {{Symbol|Affect|Enemy}}
*** Runs toward the nearest enemy hero if Sharpshooter is not learned upon cast.
** {{Symbol|Illusions}} {{Symbol|Wind-up}}
*** Winds-up Sharpshooter regardless if the illusion has enough {{M|mana}} to cast.

